---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import KitForm from '../components/KitForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free Training: The Blogs That Sell Framework"
  description="Get the free framework for writing blog posts that rank on Google AND convert readers into paying customers. Stop creating content that gets ignored."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-gradient-to-b from-primary-50 to-white">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 mb-6 text-sm font-medium bg-accent/10 text-accent-dark rounded-full">
        Free PDF Guide
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-6">
        Stop Writing Blog Posts<br class="hidden md:block" /> That Nobody Buys From
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-gray-600 mb-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        Get the exact framework for writing blog posts that rank on Google <strong>AND</strong> convert readers into paying customers.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 mb-10">
        Used by freelancers, consultants, and course creators to turn organic traffic into revenue.
      </p>

      <!-- Hero Opt-in -->
      <div class="max-w-md mx-auto">
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-xl">
          <KitForm
            buttonText="Send Me the Free Framework"
            showName={true}
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problem Section -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-8 text-center">
        Here's The Problem With "Content Marketing"
      </h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p>
          You've done everything right. You researched keywords. You wrote "valuable" content. You published consistently. You promoted on social media.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>And you got... nothing.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Maybe some traffic. Maybe a few rankings. But conversions? Sales? Clients booking calls?
        </p>
        <p>
          Crickets.
        </p>
        <p>
          Here's the uncomfortable truth nobody wants to tell you:
        </p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-primary-500 pl-6 italic">
          <p>
            Most "content marketing" advice is designed for media companies that monetize pageviews—not businesses that need to sell.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          You don't need more traffic. You don't need more "brand awareness." You don't need another 2,000-word "ultimate guide" that gets bookmarked and forgotten.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>You need blog posts that actually convert.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Solution Section -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-8 text-center">
        There's A Better Way
      </h2>
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p>
          What if every blog post you wrote was engineered—from the first sentence to the final CTA—to move readers toward becoming customers?
        </p>
        <p>
          Not through manipulation. Not through "hacks." But through the same proven persuasion principles that have powered million-dollar sales letters for over a century.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The Blogs That Sell Framework</strong> shows you exactly how to do it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What's Inside -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4 text-center">
        Inside The Free Framework, You'll Discover:
      </h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-10 text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        This isn't theory. It's a practical, step-by-step framework you can apply to your next blog post.
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-primary-100 text-primary-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
            1
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-lg mb-1">Why 95% of Blog Content Fails to Convert</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600">The fundamental mistake almost everyone makes—and exactly how to avoid it. (This one shift changes everything.)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-primary-100 text-primary-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
            2
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-lg mb-1">The 5 Direct-Response Principles for Blog Posts</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600">The same framework that powers high-converting sales letters, adapted for SEO content that ranks AND converts.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-primary-100 text-primary-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
            3
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-lg mb-1">The Buyer-Intent Keyword Hierarchy</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600">Stop targeting vanity keywords that attract tire-kickers. Learn to find the searches that signal someone is ready to buy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-primary-100 text-primary-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
            4
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-lg mb-1">The Blog Post Structure Template</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600">A plug-and-play template you can use for any post that needs to persuade. Hook, agitate, solve, convert.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 p-6 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-12 h-12 bg-primary-100 text-primary-600 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl">
            5
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-lg mb-1">The Quick-Start Checklist</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600">A printable checklist to use before publishing. Never publish a post that isn't optimized to convert again.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who It's For -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8 text-center">
        This Framework Is For You If...
      </h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {[
          "You're creating content but not seeing leads or sales",
          "You're tired of 'brand awareness' that doesn't pay bills",
          "You're a freelancer or consultant who wants inbound clients",
          "You sell courses, coaching, or high-ticket services",
          "You want to write less content but get better results",
          "You're ready to stop guessing and start converting",
        ].map((item) => (
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-4 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-green-500 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M16.707 5.293a1 1 0 010 1.414l-8 8a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 011.414-1.414L8 12.586l7.293-7.293a1 1 0 011.414 0z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-gray-700 font-medium">{item}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Social Proof Placeholder -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center">
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 italic">
        "The framework changed how I think about every piece of content I create. My blog posts finally feel like they're doing something."
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">— Framework User</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-primary-900 text-white">
    <div class="container-narrow text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-4">
        Get The Framework Free (Instant Access)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Stop creating content that gets ignored. Start writing blog posts that actually convert.
      </p>
      <div class="max-w-md mx-auto">
        <KitForm
          buttonText="Send Me the Free Framework"
          showName={true}
          variant="dark"
        />
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-6">
        Instant PDF download. No credit card required. Unsubscribe anytime.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-10 text-center">
        Questions
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            Is this really free?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">
            Yes. Enter your email and you'll get instant access to the complete PDF framework. No credit card required, no hidden charges.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            Will this work for my industry?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">
            The framework is based on timeless direct-response principles that work across industries. If you sell services, courses, consulting, coaching, or software—this applies to you.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
            What happens after I sign up?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-500 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600">
            You'll receive an email with a link to download the PDF immediately. You'll also get occasional emails with more tips and strategies—but you can unsubscribe anytime with one click.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
